<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luitpold, Prince Regent of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1821">1821</a>–<a href="/years/1912">1912</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Prince Regent Luitpold</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Luitpold was prince regent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> from 1886 until his death in 1912. A son of King Ludwig I, he took over the government when his nephew Ludwig II was declared insane and deposed, and continued as regent for Ludwig's brother Otto, who was also incapable of ruling. His long regency, the Prinzregentenzeit, was a period of prosperity and cultural flowering in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a>. His son became King Ludwig III.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luitpold-prince-regent-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="Luitpold, Prince Regent of Bavaria" width="320" height="424" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kunstverlag Franz Hanfstaengl · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Luitpold_Wittelsbach_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
